<meta type=article>
  <title | Apparatus-tag positioning fixture>
</meta>

<section | A correctly-placed body section>

The apparatus-tag positioning rule warns when `<meta>`/`<config>`/`<data>`/
`<library>` appear inside another tag's content. This section is body
content — no apparatus tags belong here. But the aside below deliberately
places a `<config>` mid-body to trigger the diagnostic.

<aside | This aside contains a misplaced apparatus tag.

<config citation-style="chicago" />

The aside continues, but the misplaced <config> got a warning and is
silently ignored at its mis-placed position (the document still renders
per the always-renders pattern).
>

<section | Surrounding content continues>

Content after the misplaced apparatus tag renders normally.
